WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.690 --> 00:00:04.870
Two more protocol and port combinations to
know about for the exam are Remote Desktop

00:00:04.870 --> 00:00:08.870
Protocol (RDP) and Secure Shell (SSH).

00:00:08.870 --> 00:00:15.329
RDP, which is used to connect one device to
another remotely, as I am doing here, runs

00:00:15.329 --> 00:00:17.510
on port 3389.

00:00:17.510 --> 00:00:24.890
SSH is often used to connect a device such
as this to a hardware device, such as a router.

00:00:24.890 --> 00:00:30.320
SSH can also connect one device to another,
which is especially the case with Linux devices.

00:00:30.320 --> 00:00:33.180
SSH runs on port 22.

00:00:33.180 --> 00:00:37.960
One more note about SSH: It is encrypted and
is thus secure.

00:00:37.960 --> 00:00:42.719
Telnet, another protocol used to connect to
devices, is not secure.

